-**Decided with the user (2026-10-21):** "Rewrite finished files". This is the user's exception to "sequestered files never change", for **finished** items only, in this PR. Every `done/` item's `check.sh` (122 files, both roots; no finished item keeps an `acceptance/` folder, since `done` promotes it) has its moved paths rewritten to their new locations, so it passes again when run by hand and no longer needs the forwarders. Unfinished items' sequestered files never change: they move as `R100` renames and run through the forwarders. The rewrite is one function, `rewrites.paths` in c0114's acceptance folder (`rewrites.luau`), applied in the edits commit, never in the renames-only one (JC1 still holds):
-- every moved path of §1 becomes its new place: `scripts/tracker/` to `z-nile/engine/`; `scripts/lib/{ac.sh,fence.sh,par.sh,replace-file.pl,git-hooks,sh.luau,graph.luau,changed.luau}` to `z-nile/lib/`; `scripts/{check.sh,setup.sh,ci-verify.sh,affected,vendor}` to `z-nile/`; `tracker/templates` and `tracker/compaction.txt` to `z-nile/`;
