-### 7. Guards fail closed
-- `z-nile/lib/ac.sh`: no `z-nile/lib/fence.sh` beside it: "ac.sh: <root>/z-nile/lib/fence.sh is missing: refusing to run checks without the repository guards", exit 1, before any check. The old "a fixture holding only ac.sh" exception is gone: such a fixture now copies `z-nile/lib/` whole (c0034's override).
-- `scripts/lib/ac.sh` forwarder: no target, "ac.sh: z-nile/lib/ac.sh is missing", exit 1.
-- `pickman_guarded <dir>` (in `fence.sh`) answers with one line and exit 0: `guarded` when the repository holding `<dir>` is one the guards protect, `unguarded` when it is not. Anything else (it can't read the repository, a non-zero exit, no line, another line) is no answer.
-- `guarded()` in `main.luau` runs `source z-nile/lib/fence.sh && pickman_guarded "$PWD"` (a missing file is reported as "z-nile/lib/fence.sh is missing") and publishes only when the result is exit 0 with exactly `unguarded`. Every other outcome counts as guarded: a missing or unparseable `fence.sh`, a missing `pickman_guarded`, a failing lookup, another answer, a `bash` that can't start. It then prints "not publishing: cannot ask z-nile/lib/fence.sh whether a check runs in <cwd> (exit <n>: <stderr>)", and on `guarded` "not publishing: <cwd> is protected by the repository guards (a check run)". Either way the command goes on as with `PICKMAN_PUBLISH=0`. (A guard's "no" is one explicit answer: lesson architecture/guard-no-is-explicit.)
-- `pickman_fence`: the hooks default to `$here/z-nile/lib/git-hooks`. If neither the inherited `PICKMAN_FENCE_HOOKS` nor that folder has executable `reference-transaction` and `pre-push`, it refuses ("fence: no ref guard at <dir> ...; refusing"), except inside a jailed spec run, where the kernel already refuses every write to the repository and no hook was ever set. The waiver rests on all three of the runner's markers at once: `PICKMAN_TEST_JAIL=sandbox-exec`, `PICKMAN_FENCE_SPECS=1`, and the checkout lying under `$PICKMAN_TEST_FENCE/.cache/` (the run's own fixtures). **Decided with the user (2026-10-21):** accepted as guessed ("the jail waiver, under all three markers"). The user kept this jail exception, narrowed to the runner's markers: without it every fixture that sources the fence would have to carry the hooks folder.
-- `tests/lib/fence.luau` sources `z-nile/lib/fence.sh` with `. file && ...`, so a runner without it stops before any spec (unchanged behaviour, new path, now pinned by AC7).
-- A missing registry refuses like a bad one (G4, §2): no lookup of the roots falls back to a guessed set.
