-- **The execution window.** From step 2 until c0114 merges, its branch has the registry while origin/main has none and keeps raising `tracker/next` (lesson ticket-prep/design-the-execution-window: a branch never edits shared state main keeps writing; origin moves it when the branch lands). Then:
-  - ids in the window: the branch's engine reserves none (it publishes nothing, G4), and makes none offline either: `new issue` and `new raft` refuse on the branch while origin/main has no registry, `PICKMAN_PUBLISH=0` included ("capture from the main checkout until it does, never offline here"; an offline id would come from the local `tracker/next`, the number main's next capture takes), and their refusal no longer suggests `PICKMAN_PUBLISH=0`; so every id is made on main by the main checkout's old engine, from origin's `tracker/next`, and reaches the branch by merge. A capture or a lesson issue in the window is made from the main checkout (the tracker skill's backlog capture, `scripts/tracker.sh new issue ...` there); an emergent issue the raft needs is filed the same way into the backlog, named in the PR description, and moved into `z-nile/.tracker/` by step 9 if it is tooling work; it does not join R0043. No id collision can arise between the branch and main: the branch creates no item, and its moves keep every id. So execute-raft Phase 6 step 2's "renumber colliding IDs" never applies to this raft (and `renumber` refuses on the branch, window.spec pins it); `./zn audit` after each merge would report a `duplicate` if that ever stopped being true;
-  - the branch never changes `tracker/next`, so every merge of `origin/main` (plain `git`, `./zn sync`, a publish's merge-back, GitHub's own after `done`) takes main's counter without a conflict; nothing in step 9 or execute-raft Phase 5 changes for it;
-  - `./zn audit` on the branch gives `warning counter-unmigrated` (not an error: AC12 stays green) until the first publish after landing moves the counter (§5);
-  - `refuseStale` compares `z-nile/compaction.txt`; in the window origin has none, so a compaction there would go unseen, but compaction refuses while any branch changes `tracker/`, which c0114's does from step 2 on.
